aarch64: use prfum for the negative prefetch offset

copy_linux_aarch64.s prefetches backwards with a scaled prfm:

  prfm    pldl1keep, [s, #-256]

The scaled form only encodes non-negative multiples of 8, so clang's
integrated assembler rejects it:

  copy_linux_aarch64.s:332:32: error: index must be a multiple of 8 in
      range [0, 32760].

The unscaled form, prfum, is what takes a negative offset -- and the very same
file already uses it for the matching prefetch a hundred lines earlier, so this
just makes the two agree. GNU as accepts either spelling, which is why it went
unnoticed upstream.

diff --git a/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/copy_linux_aarch64.s b/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/copy_linux_aarch64.s
index 6d00d9f..e7f9215 100644
--- a/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/copy_linux_aarch64.s
+++ b/hotspot/src/os_cpu/linux_aarch64/vm/copy_linux_aarch64.s
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@ unal_bwd_copy:
         blo     unal_bwd_copy_drain
 
 unal_bwd_copy_again:
-        prfm    pldl1keep, [s, #-256]
+        prfum   pldl1keep, [s, #-256]
         str     t1, [d, #-8]
         stp     t3, t0, [d, #-24]
         ldp     t0, t1, [s, #-16]
